    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-20T11:16:18+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T11:16:18+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T00:46:18Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T00:46:18Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system in the Bight will drift southeast as the associated trough crosses eastern South Australia clears before clearing later Friday. A weak high pressure system briefly moves across southern SA later Friday before a trough and cold front then move into the west from Saturday evening and cross the rest of SA on Sunday. A high will then push in behind the front and will move across the Bight early next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the late morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds near the eastern border. Winds northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 35 to 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly in the morning then tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 26 with daytime temperatures reaching 35 to 42.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Yunta, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of raised dust north of Leigh Creek in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day then tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 21 to 29 with daytime temperatures reaching 38 to 46.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 30 to 45 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 28 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
